				<h2>Behaviour</h2>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>The picture is the player.</strong> Play opens nothing: the frame changes shape where it stands — 16:9, or 9:16 on a phone — and the film plays inside it. Its rectangle is tweened with the Web Animations API, so nothing stretches.</li>
					<li><strong>Nothing loads from YouTube until play is pressed</strong> (and then from the no-cookie domain). The iframe is destroyed on close. <kbd>Esc</kbd> closes.</li>
					<li><strong>Responsive by container, not viewport:</strong> ≤1080, ≤880 (tablet) and ≤640 (phone) of the hero's <em>own</em> width — so it is right beside an open nav, a rail, or none.</li>
					<li><strong>Reduced motion</strong> stops the background loop (in CSS and in JS, since a hidden video still decodes), the ticker and the arrival stagger.</li>
					<li><strong>Dark mode</strong> inverts the wash rather than swapping files: one loop, both schemes.</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>Depends on</h2>
				<p>Tokens (<code>--im-*</code>, <code>--im-text-*</code>, <code>--im-space</code>, <code>--im-radius-2xl</code>, <code>--im-font-pixel</code>), the <code>.im-btn</code> and <code>.im-subscribe</code> components, and six icons. No library.</p>

